## Fork-only integration

`@ayme-dev/playwright-lite/internal` exports `captureAriaSnapshot`, `isPlaywrightLiteLocator`, and `resolveLocatorElements`, plus the capture result type. This entry preserves WebMCP's existing dual ARIA capture and locator-to-DOM identity contract. It is not part of the personal upstream API or WebMCP's public API. The root exports only `createPage` and `CreatePageOptions`; locator brands and implementation classes remain private.

The compatibility corpus stays pinned to stock Playwright {{playwrightVersion}} in `tests/upstream/corpus.ts`. Injected code is generated separately from `ayme-labs/playwright@b25d782e3fbdf21abdae60e974e49b78ca07e828`, selected in `scripts/generate-injected.mjs`. The fork patch adds dual capture without adding POM availability policy or changing evaluation semantics.

## Installation

playwright-lite is pre-1.0; APIs may change. Install the fork as a Git dependency pinned to an exact commit of `ayme-labs/playwright-lite`.

Git installation runs `prepare` to build the checked-in generated sources in `build/generated`. Unlike upstream, this fork commits them and hash-checks them during builds, so consumers do not clone Playwright or run its generator. Building from Git uses the contributor toolchain (Node.js 24, pnpm 11.24.0), not the minimum Node version of the built package. WebMCP explicitly allows this dependency's build and bundles the result into its distribution. Its consumers do not install or build the fork.

The packed browser library requires Node.js 20 or newer.

Maintainers regenerate the sources with `pnpm generate:injected` and verify them with `pnpm generate:check`. Review artifact hash changes before updating the build pin in `build/playwrightInjectedPlugin.ts`. [docs/fork/SYNC.md](docs/fork/SYNC.md) describes how the fork follows upstream.

